messages:
irene: quick PSA 1: PR #9876 added a JS snippet in docs/error-ref/429.md that fails the snippet harness. CI shows a header mismatch + a broken link to sdk/js/retries.md. can someone take a look?

ben: on it. failing test: KeyError for 'x-retry-after' 1 runtime now sends 'x-retry-after-ms'. link moved when we split sdk examples.

tao: I reviewed the PR; i accidentally grabbed the old retry example. i'll fix the link. for snippet, suggest we normalize headers so examples are resilient.

ben: proposed minimal change (JS):

```js
// prefer ms header, fallback to seconds
const hdrMs = response.headers['x-retry-after-ms'];
const hdrS = response.headers['x-retry-after'];
let waitMs = 0;
if (hdrMs) waitMs = parseInt(hdrMs, 10);
else if (hdrS) waitMs = Math.round(parseFloat(hdrS) * 1000);
else waitMs = 200 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 200);
await sleep(waitMs);
```

ben: also add a one-line note above: "Examples accept both 'x-retry-after-ms' and 'x-retry-after' for backwards compatibility."

tao: +1. i'll update the link and add the compatibility note. small ask: can we move the long-hosted repro to docs/samples/429-mock.md and change CI snippet tests to use the mock server? hitting prod for deterministic tests is flaky.

qa-bot: failing snippet test logged: docs/error-ref/429.md snippet#1 1 see https://ci.internal/redwood-docs/9876/logs

irene: agreed re: mock. tao, if you push the link + header-norm patch i can adjust the CI test to point to docs/tests/mock_server.js. that will make the harness deterministic. also, can we add a tiny table summarizing cause -> quick action (surge -> backoff; sustained QPS -> route to dedicated; too-large prompt -> trim oldest messages) so support has a TL;DR?

tao: pushed branch docs/fix-429-snippet -> PR #9876 with link + note + snippet.

